<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyrylo Rozumovsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1728">1728</a>–<a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Kirill Razumovsky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyrylo Rozumovsky was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossack-hetmanate">Cossack Hetmanate</a> in Left-bank <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, from 1750 to 1764. The younger brother of Empress Elizabeth's favourite Oleksiy Rozumovsky, he also served as president of the Russian Academy of Sciences. He governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hlukhiv">Hlukhiv</a> and Baturyn and tried to reform <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> courts and administration, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a> forced him to resign in 1764.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyrylo-rozumovsky.jpg" alt="Kyrylo Rozumovsky" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Tocqué · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirill_Razumovsky_Tokke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
